From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gleb Pesin <dormancygrace@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 20:35:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: mediatek: honor disabled RX checksum trust

Backport the RX checksum feature check from the Linux MT7620
preparation. The parser may remain active after ethtool disables RX
checksum offload. Only mark the skb CHECKSUM_UNNECESSARY when the
netdevice advertises NETIF_F_RXCSUM as enabled; otherwise let the stack
verify the checksum.

Assisted-by: Codex (OpenAI GPT-6)
Signed-off-by: Gleb Pesin <dormancygrace@gmail.com>
---

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.c
@@ -2757,7 +2757,8 @@ static int mtk_poll_rx(struct napi_struc
 			rxdcsum = &trxd.rxd4;
 		}
 
-		if (*rxdcsum & eth->soc->rx.dma_l4_valid)
+		if ((netdev->features & NETIF_F_RXCSUM) &&
+		    (*rxdcsum & eth->soc->rx.dma_l4_valid))
 			skb->ip_summed = CHECKSUM_UNNECESSARY;
 		else
 			skb_checksum_none_assert(skb);
